At the moment something like `select (3 < languages) as multi_language, count(*) from test_emp group by multi_language` doesn't work.  The exception is not entirely accurate in my opinion and the ES query used  in this scenario is very similar with the one from https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/34400.

```
{
  "size": 0,
  "aggs": {
    "NAME": {
      "composite": {
        "sources": [
          {
            "product": {
              "terms": {
                "script": {
                  "source": "doc['languages'].value > 3",
                  "lang": "painless"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
